    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Serum lactate and ketones must also be checked, usually using VBG and point of care testing. The former can indicate lactic acidosis related to e.g. sepsis, and the latter will exclude significant ketonaemia (ß-hydroxybutyrate <1.0 mmol/L)." ;
