    dmo:evidenceQuote "Establish monitoring regime appropriate to the individual – generally hourly blood glucose, Na+, K+, urea and calculated osmolality [(2xNa+) + glucose + urea] for the first 6 hours, then 2 hourly osmolality if the response is satisfactory (i.e. a fall of 3.0-8.0 mOsm/kg/hr)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

