    rdfs:label "Initial fluid replacement with 0.9% sodium chloride solution with potassium added as required" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "40" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "initial-fluid-replacement-with-0-9-sodium-chloride-solution-with-potassium-added-as-required" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "As the majority of electrolyte losses are sodium, chloride and potassium, the initial fluid replacement of choice should be 0.9% sodium chloride solution with potassium added as required." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "As the majority of electrolyte losses are sodium, chloride and potassium, the initial fluid replacement of choice should be 0.9% sodium chloride solution with potassium added as required (40)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/initial-target-glucose-of-10-15-mmol-l-until-person-is-eating-and-drinking-normally> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Initial target glucose of 10–15 mmol/L until person is eating and drinking normally" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "initial-target-glucose-of-10-15-mmol-l-until-person-is-eating-and-drinking-normally" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "An initial target glucose of between 10-15 mmol/L is a reasonable goal until the person is eating and drinking normally, and then an individual target glucose (if appropriate 6–10 mmol/L) should be set by the diabetes specialist team and the person with diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• an initial target glucose of between 10-15 mmol/L is a reasonable goal until the person is eating and drinking normally, and then an individual target glucose (if appropriate 6–10 mmol/L) should be set by the diabetes specialist team and the person with diabetes" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/initiate-iv-fluids-and-friii-for-mixed-hhs-dka> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Initiate IV Fluids and FRIII for Mixed HHS/DKA" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults admitted with HHS and showing signs of mixed HHS/DKA (significant hypovolaemia, hyperosmolality, pH<7.3, and ketones >3.0 mmol/L)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "initiate-iv-fluids-and-friii-for-mixed-hhs-dka" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Commence IV fluids and FRIII of 0.1 units/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Commence IV fluids and FRIII of 0.1 units/kg/hr" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-dose-adjustment-based-on-glucose-fall-rate> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Dose Adjustment Based on Glucose Fall Rate" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS with blood glucose falling at < 5.0 mmol/L per hour" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-dose-adjustment-based-on-glucose-fall-rate" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "if the blood glucose is falling at < 5.0 mmol/L per hour, then check fluid balance. If the fluid balance is inadequate, then increase the rate of infusion of 0.9% sodium chloride solution. If the fluid balance is adequate, then commence an FRIII at 0.05 units/kg/hr, or if already running, increase the rate to 0.1 units/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "if the blood glucose is falling at < 5.0 mmol/L per hour, then check fluid balance. If the fluid balance is inadequate, then increase the rate of infusion of 0.9% sodium chloride solution. If the fluid balance is adequate, then commence an FRIII at 0.05 units/kg/hr, or if already running, increase the rate to 0.1 units/kg/hr" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-dose-for-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Dose for HHS" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-dose-for-hhs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "the recommended insulin dose is a FRIII given at 0.05 units/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "the recommended insulin dose is a FRIII given at 0.05 units/kg/hr" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-infusion-in-hhs-with-ketonaemia-but-not-acidotic> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Infusion in HHS With Ketonaemia but Not Acidotic" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS and ketonaemia (blood ketones 3ß-hydroxybutyrate >1.0 - ≤3.0 mmol/L or urine ketones < 2+) and not acidotic (venous pH >7.3 and bicarbonate >15.0 mmol/L)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-infusion-in-hhs-with-ketonaemia-but-not-acidotic" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If there is HHS and ketonaemia (blood ketones 3ß-hydroxybutyrate >1.0 - ≤3.0 mmol/L or urine ketones < 2+) and not acidotic (venous pH >7.3 and bicarbonate >15.0 mmol/L) then use 0.05 units/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If there is HHS and ketonaemia (blood ketones 3ß-hydroxybutyrate >1.0 - ≤3.0 mmol/L or urine ketones < 2+) and not acidotic (venous pH >7.3 and bicarbonate >15.0 mmol/L) then use 0.05 units/kg/hr" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-infusion-in-hhs-without-significant-ketonaemia> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Infusion in HHS Without Significant Ketonaemia" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS without significant ketonaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-infusion-in-hhs-without-significant-ketonaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "if significant ketonaemia is not present do NOT start an intravenous insulin infusion" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "if significant ketonaemia is not present do NOT start an intravenous insulin infusion" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-infusion-in-mixed-dka-and-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Infusion in Mixed DKA and HHS" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with mixed DKA and HHS (significant ketonaemia (3ß-hydroxybutyrate >3.0 mmol/L) or ketonuria (≥ 2+) with a pH <7.3 and bicarbonate <15 mmol/L)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-infusion-in-mixed-dka-and-hhs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If there is significant ketonaemia (3ß-hydroxybutyrate >3.0 mmol/L) or ketonuria (≥ 2+) with a pH <7.3 and bicarbonate <15 mmol/L (i.e. mixed DKA and HHS) and use the DKA guideline at 0.1 units/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If there is significant ketonaemia (3ß-hydroxybutyrate >3.0 mmol/L) or ketonuria (≥ 2+) with a pH <7.3 and bicarbonate <15 mmol/L (i.e. mixed DKA and HHS) and use the DKA guideline at 0.1 units/kg/hr" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-syringe-use-in-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
