<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/substitute-0-45-sodium-chloride-solution-if-osmolality-is-not-declining-despite-adequate-0-9-nacl> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Substitute 0.45% sodium chloride solution if osmolality is not declining despite adequate 0.9% NaCl" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "substitute-0-45-sodium-chloride-solution-if-osmolality-is-not-declining-despite-adequate-0-9-nacl" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Ideally, people will recover quickly enough to replace the water deficit themselves by taking fluids orally. However, if the osmolality is no longer declining despite adequate fluid replacement with 0.9% sodium chloride solution AND an adequate rate of fall of plasma glucose is not being achieved, then 0.45% sodium chloride solution should be substituted." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "However, if the osmolality is no longer declining despite adequate fluid replacement with 0.9% sodium chloride solution AND an adequate rate of fall of plasma glucose is not being achieved, then 0.45% sodium chloride solution should be substituted." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/switch-to-0-45-sodium-chloride-if-osmolality-increasing-and-fluid-balance-adequate> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Switch to 0.45% sodium chloride if osmolality increasing and fluid balance adequate" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "switch-to-0-45-sodium-chloride-if-osmolality-increasing-and-fluid-balance-adequate" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If the osmolality is increasing and fluid balance adequate, then consider switching to 0.45% sodium chloride at same infusion rate" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• If the osmolality is increasing and fluid balance adequate, then consider switching to 0.45% sodium chloride at same infusion rate" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/switch-to-hypotonic-fluids-in-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Switch to Hypotonic Fluids in HHS" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults with diabetes affected by Hyperosmolar Hyperglycaemic State (HHS)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "switch-to-hypotonic-fluids-in-hhs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "only switch to 0.45% sodium chloride solution if the osmolality is not declining despite adequate positive fluid balance. An initial rise in sodium is expected due to the reversal of relative pseudohyponatraemia in the context of hyperglycaemia and is not itself an indication for hypotonic fluids. The rate of change of serum sodium should not exceed 10 mmol in 24 hours" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "only switch to 0.45% sodium chloride solution if the osmolality is not declining despite adequate positive fluid balance. An initial rise in sodium is expected due to the reversal of relative pseudohyponatraemia in the context of hyperglycaemia and is not itself an indication for hypotonic fluids. The rate of change of serum sodium should not exceed 10 mmol in 24 hours" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/switch-to-vriii-with-10-glucose-and-0-15-kcl-at-125-ml-hr-if-biochemical-markers-have-normalised-and-patient-still-not-eating-and-drinking> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Switch to VRIII with 10% Glucose and 0.15% KCl at 125 ml/hr if biochemical markers have normalised and patient still not eating and drinking" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "switch-to-vriii-with-10-glucose-and-0-15-kcl-at-125-ml-hr-if-biochemical-markers-have-normalised-and-patient-still-not-eating-and-drinking" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Switch from FRIII to VRIII with 10% Glucose with 0.15% KCl (i.e. 20 mmol/l) at 125 ml/hr IF Biochemical markers have normalised (osmolality <300 mOsm/kg) and STILL not eating and drinking" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Switch from FRIII to VRIII with 10% Glucose with 0.15% KCl (i.e. 20 mmol/l) at 125 ml/hr IF Biochemical markers have normalised (osmolality <300 mOsm/kg) and STILL not eating and drinking" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/switching-from-insulin-to-oral-or-subcutaneous-glucose-lowering-drugs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Switching from Insulin to Oral or Subcutaneous Glucose Lowering Drugs" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Those with previously undiagnosed diabetes or well controlled on oral agents" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "switching-from-insulin-to-oral-or-subcutaneous-glucose-lowering-drugs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Conditional" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "For those with previously undiagnosed diabetes or who were well controlled on oral agents, switching from insulin to the appropriate oral or subcutaneous glucose lowering drugs should be considered after a period of stability. This may take weeks or months." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For those with previously undiagnosed diabetes or who were well controlled on oral agents, switching from insulin to the appropriate oral or subcutaneous glucose lowering drugs should be considered after a period of stability. This may take weeks or months." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/target-glucose-range-for-hhs-management> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Target Glucose Range for HHS Management" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults admitted with HHS" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "target-glucose-range-for-hhs-management" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Aim for a target glucose of 10.0 – 15.0 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Aim for a target glucose of 10.0 – 15.0 mmol/L" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/target-rate-of-glucose-fall-in-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Target Rate of Glucose Fall in HHS" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "target-rate-of-glucose-fall-in-hhs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "a fall of glucose at a rate of up to 5.0 mmol/L per hour is ideal" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "a fall of glucose at a rate of up to 5.0 mmol/L per hour is ideal" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/the-individual-should-be-encouraged-to-drink-as-soon-as-it-is-safe-to-do-so> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "The individual should be encouraged to drink as soon as it is safe to do so" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "the-individual-should-be-encouraged-to-drink-as-soon-as-it-is-safe-to-do-so" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "the individual should be encouraged to drink as soon as it is safe to do so and an accurate fluid balance chart should be maintained until IV fluids are no longer required" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "the individual should be encouraged to drink as soon as it is safe to do so and an accurate fluid balance chart should be maintained until IV fluids are no longer required" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/the-individual-should-be-steadily-recovering-beginning-to-eat-and-drink-and-the-biochemistry-is-as-it-was-prior-to-the-acute-episode> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "The individual should be steadily recovering, beginning to eat and drink, and the biochemistry is as it was prior to the acute episode" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "the-individual-should-be-steadily-recovering-beginning-to-eat-and-drink-and-the-biochemistry-is-as-it-was-prior-to-the-acute-episode" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "The individual should be steadily recovering, beginning to eat and drink, and the biochemistry is as it was prior to the acute episode" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• The individual should be steadily recovering, beginning to eat and drink, and the biochemistry is as it was prior to the acute episode" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/therapeutic-anticoagulation-in-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Therapeutic Anticoagulation in HHS" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "therapeutic-anticoagulation-in-hhs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "There are no data to recommend that this advice be extended to therapeutic anticoagulation. Full, therapeutic anticoagulation should only be considered in those with suspected thrombosis or acute coronary syndrome." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There are no data to recommend that this advice be extended to therapeutic anticoagulation. Full, therapeutic anticoagulation should only be considered in those with suspected thrombosis or acute coronary syndrome." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/timing-of-insulin-initiation-after-fluid-resuscitation> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Timing of Insulin Initiation After Fluid Resuscitation" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with HHS after initial fluid resuscitation" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "timing-of-insulin-initiation-after-fluid-resuscitation" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "once the glucose has ceased to fall following initial fluid resuscitation, reassessment of fluid intake and evaluation of renal function must be undertaken. Insulin may be started at this point, or, if already in place, the infusion rate increased by 1.0 unit/hr." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "once the glucose has ceased to fall following initial fluid resuscitation, reassessment of fluid intake and evaluation of renal function must be undertaken. Insulin may be started at this point, or, if already in place, the infusion rate increased by 1.0 unit/hr." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/treat-underlying-cause-if-known> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Treat underlying cause if known" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "treat-underlying-cause-if-known" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Treat underlying cause if known" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• Treat underlying cause if known" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-0-45-n-saline-only-if-osmolality-is-not-falling-despite-adequate-fluids> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use 0.45% N/Saline only if osmolality is not falling despite adequate fluids" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-0-45-n-saline-only-if-osmolality-is-not-falling-despite-adequate-fluids" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "ONLY Use 0.45% N/Saline if osmolality is not falling despite adequate fluids" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "ONLY Use 0.45% N/Saline if osmolality is not falling despite adequate fluids" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-0-9-sodium-chloride-solution-as-principle-fluid-for-volume-restoration> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use 0.9% sodium chloride solution as principle fluid for volume restoration" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-0-9-sodium-chloride-solution-as-principle-fluid-for-volume-restoration" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "0.9% sodium chloride solution should be used as the principle fluid to restore circulating volume and reverse dehydration because it is relatively hypotonic compared to the serum in someone with HHS." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• rapid changes in osmolality may be harmful. 0.9% sodium chloride solution should be used as the principle fluid to restore circulating volume and reverse dehydration because it is relatively hypotonic compared to the serum in someone with HHS" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-0-9-sodium-chloride-solution-for-fluid-replacement> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use 0.9% sodium chloride solution for fluid replacement" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-0-9-sodium-chloride-solution-for-fluid-replacement" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Using 0.9% sodium chloride solution aim to give a further 0.5-1 litre/hr depending on clinical assessment of dehydration vs. risk of precipitating heart failure. The target is to achieve positive fluid balance of 2-3 litres by 6 hours" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "o Using 0.9% sodium chloride solution aim to give a further 0.5-1 litre/hr depending on clinical assessment of dehydration vs. risk of precipitating heart failure. The target is to achieve positive fluid balance of 2-3 litres by 6 hours" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-cautious-fluid-replacement-in-low-weight-or-high-risk-patients> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use cautious fluid replacement in low-weight or high-risk patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-cautious-fluid-replacement-in-low-weight-or-high-risk-patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Fluid replacement should be adjusted for those who are <50 kg in body weight or with pre-existing heart and renal disease. More cautious fluid replacement is necessary e.g. 0.25 ml/kg/hr as recommended by NICE (13)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• Fluid replacement should be adjusted for those who are <50 kg in body weight or with pre-existing heart and renal disease. More cautious fluid replacement is necessary e.g. 0.25 ml/kg/hr as recommended by NICE (13)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_06_management_of_hhs_in_adults> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-0-45-n-saline-in-hhs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
